.TH LIBMPQ__ARCHIVE_SIGNATURES 3 2026-09-18 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__archive_signatures \- detect weak and strong archive signatures
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__archive_signatures("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "signatures"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Detects structurally valid signatures on the reader \fIarchive\fP and writes
a bitmask to \fI*signatures\fP. The mask may contain
\fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_WEAK\fP for an internal \fB(signature)\fP member and
\fBLIBMPQ_SIGNATURE_STRONG\fP for an external NGIS trailer. Zero means
neither is present. Internal weak signatures are also available in
MPQE-wrapped MPQs; no external strong-signature transport is defined for
MPQE.
.PP
This call checks storage structure, not cryptographic authenticity.
Use \fBlibmpq__archive_verify\fP(3) with a caller-supplied public key to
verify one detected signature.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns \fBLIBMPQ_SUCCESS\fP and sets \fI*signatures\fP on success,
including when the mask is zero. A non-NULL output is initialized to zero
before validation. On failure it returns a negative libmpq error; callers
must not use the partial mask.
.SH ERRORS
NULL required arguments return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST\fP; writer handles
return \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED\fP. Malformed signature storage
returns \fBLIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT\fP; reader or I/O errors may propagate.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_verify (3),
.BR libmpq__archive_sign (3),
.BR libmpq__patch_sign (3)
